rther development\n\nReason: Discarding W6 maintains the highest winning potential by keeping the bamboo tiles B5, B5, B6, B7 together. This allows me to wait for B4 (3 remaining) to form a chow [B4,B5,B6] while keeping a pair of B5 and B7 for final hand completion. W6 is isolated and contributes nothing to potential winning patterns.\n\nAnswer: Play W6"}
